<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://www.unesco.org/en/days/philosophy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">World Philosophy Day</a>, created by the United Nations Educational, Scientific, and Cultural Organization (UNESCO), celebrates “the enduring value of philosophy for the development of human thought, for each culture and for each individual.”</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">UNESCO&#8217;s theme for <a href="https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/world-philosophy-day-2026?hub=66761">this year&#8217;s World Philosophy Day</a> is &#8220;How can we coexist in a world in crises?&#8221;, with emphasis on issues related to migration, climate, artificial intelligence, and health.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Some philosophy departments take advantage of the day to promote philosophy, present interactive programs, or put on philosophy events (see the comments on <a href="https://dailynous.com/2025/11/14/world-philosophy-day-is-next-thursday/">this previous post</a>, for example).</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Is your department planning something to mark the day? If so, let us know about it in the comments&#8212;it&#8217;s not too late to provide inspiration for other departments looking for ideas.</p>
